  {
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "If we add `.to(..., rounding_mode=foo)` then we need an implementation of that for eager, and yes, it should be understood by inductor, but we can't introduce functionality that purportedly exists outside compile, but doesn't really...\n\nThe main issue I have with NV's stochastic rounding (and I'm not sure if it's the same issue you're alluding to, or a tangential-but-separate one) is not that we can't expose it in a clean, generic way, it's that you'd fundamentally get different results when doing scalar rounding vs. vectorized rounding due to different uses of random bits.",
