    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "@ngimel it's still icky :D \n\nTo try and summarize:\n* General alignment on adding a `rounding_mode = str | None` argument to `aten.to`.\n  * Eager mode + inductor support.\n* Non-stochastic roundings are comparatively simple. They might need some work in inductor to support, but fine.\n  * Potentially some HW-dependent support (like `T -> e8m0-RU`)\n* Stochastic rounding is more nuanced.\n  * Conceptually ok with sparse HW & SW support (read: maybe GB200 only right now, contiguous, `x.numel() % 4 == 0`)\n  * Still need some notion of how to pass RNG into DSLs & keep consistent w/PyT generator(s).\n\n",
